wire.refusal:
A stream refused before it opens answers an HTTP error status with the same content type and one frame: `event: error
data: {"error": "<sentence>"}

`, then closes. 400 (bad request), 401 (sync: no or invalid token), 404 (device or merge: a code the site never issued — see `expected`), 429 (too many attempts or streams from this address), 502 (the site did not answer the relay), 503 (the relay is at capacity).
